# ========================
# Session artifacts — MUST stay last
# ========================
# `!*.md` above (the "Keep documentation" block) un-ignores every .md in the
# tree, and gitignore resolves by LAST matching rule, so it silently defeated
# the `.claude/agent-outputs/**` rule near the top of this file: `git add -A`
# would have swept in 69 subagent report files. Re-assert the ignore here,
# after the negation, and keep these rules at the end of the file.
.claude/agent-outputs/**
!.claude/agent-outputs/
!.claude/agent-outputs/*/
!.claude/agent-outputs/*/.gitkeep

# Conversation transcripts and hook-written backups at any depth. A 125MB
# transcript once reached a commit this way because the session cwd had drifted
# and the hook wrote into crates/yu-server/src/.claude/backups/.
**/.claude/backups/**
**/.claude/session-state/**
**/.claude/*.jsonl

# Local settings backups written by tooling next to the (already ignored)
# settings.local.json. Without this, `git add -A` sweeps them into a commit.
.claude/settings.local.json.bak*

# Other agents' scratch worktrees. These hold partial copies of this very repo,
# so a blind `git add -A` commits a stale duplicate of crates/ under them.
.claire/

# Runtime databases. `gateway.sqlite` is created in the repo root by the local
# gateway and was committed once by an over-broad `git add -A`.
gateway.sqlite
gateway.sqlite-wal
gateway.sqlite-shm

# Groups index cache. `GroupsIndexCache` writes this into its cache_dir, which
# lands under crates/yu-server/ when the parity harness runs from there.
groups_index.json

# Prebuilt PDFium, fetched by scripts/fetch_pdfium.sh (pinned release + sha256).
# Not committed: ~7.3 MB per platform, and the script makes it reproducible.
vendor/pdfium/

# fast mode: project-local Rust toolchain (scripts/internal/rust_toolchain.py)
.rust-toolchain/

# CocoIndex Code (ccc) local index.
/.cocoindex_code/
